NNAAMMEE
     zzffss__pprreeppaarree__ddiisskk — special script that gets run before bringing a disk
     into a pool

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     zzffss__pprreeppaarree__ddiisskk is an optional script that gets called by libzfs before
     bringing a disk into a pool.  It can be modified by the user to run what‐
     ever commands are necessary to prepare a disk for inclusion into the
     pool.  For example, users can add lines to zzffss__pprreeppaarree__ddiisskk to do things
     like update the drive's firmware or check the drive's health.
     zzffss__pprreeppaarree__ddiisskk is optional and can be removed if not needed.  libzfs
     will look for the script at /usr/libexec/zfs/zfs_prepare_disk.

   PPrrooppeerrttiieess
     zzffss__pprreeppaarree__ddiisskk will be passed the following environment variables:

     PPOOOOLL__NNAAMMEE            Name of the pool
     VVDDEEVV__PPAATTHH            Path to the disk (like /dev/sda)
     VVDDEEVV__PPRREEPPAARREE         Reason why the disk is being prepared for inclusion
                          ('create', 'add', 'replace', or 'autoreplace').
                          This can be useful if you only want the script to be
                          run under certain actions.
     VVDDEEVV__UUPPAATTHH           Path to one of the underlying devices for the disk.
                          For multipath this would return one of the /dev/sd*
                          paths to the disk.  If the device is not a device
                          mapper device, then VVDDEEVV__UUPPAATTHH just returns the same
                          value as VVDDEEVV__PPAATTHH
     VVDDEEVV__EENNCC__SSYYSSFFSS__PPAATTHH  Path to the disk's enclosure sysfs path, if
                          available

     Note that some of these variables may have a blank value.  PPOOOOLL__NNAAMMEE is
     blank at pool creation time, for example.

EENNVVIIRROONNMMEENNTT
     zzffss__pprreeppaarree__ddiisskk runs with a limited $PATH.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     zzffss__pprreeppaarree__ddiisskk should return 0 on success, non-zero otherwise.  If non-
     zero is returned, the disk will not be included in the pool.

